export const INVESTMENT_MD = "**DRAFT FOR LEGAL REVIEW. NOT FOR SIGNATURE.**\n\nThis Agreement is made on the Investment Date between **{{company}}**, operating as CarmaCars (the \"**Company**\"), and the investor named in Schedule A (the \"**Investor**\").\n\n## 1. Definitions\n\n**1.1** In this Agreement:\n\n- \"**Invested Amount**\": the amount the Investor paid to the Company as recorded in Schedule A, plus Returns reinvested under section 4, less amounts redeemed or bought under section 7.\n- \"**Investment**\": all of the Investor's rights under this Agreement.\n- \"**Investment Date**\": the date in Schedule A on which the Company received the Invested Amount in cleared funds.\n- \"**Lockup Period**\": the six months from the Investment Date to the day before the \"**Lockup End Date**\" in Schedule A.\n- \"**Other Investor**\": any other holder of an investment in the Company on substantially this form.\n- \"**Payment Date**\": the 15th day of the month after a Return Month.\n- \"**Redemption Price**\": the Invested Amount being redeemed plus unpaid Return earned on it before the date the Company pays it (the \"**Redemption Date**\").\n- \"**Return Month**\": each calendar month, or part of one, from the Lockup End Date to the Redemption Date.\n- \"**Securities Laws**\": the securities legislation of Ontario and of any other Canadian jurisdiction that applies to the Investor.\n- \"**Senior Obligations**\": all amounts the Company owes at any time to secured lenders and lessors, governments, employees and contractors, vehicle owners under its owner program, renters, insurers and ordinary-course trade creditors.\n- \"**Transfer**\": to sell, assign, pledge, charge or otherwise dispose of any part of the Investment, directly or indirectly.\n- \"**Yearly Percentage**\": the yearly return percentage in Schedule A.\n\n**1.2** Amounts are in Canadian dollars. Schedule A prevails on the Investor's amounts, percentage and dates.\n\n## 2. The Investment\n\n**2.1 Investment.** The Investor invests the Invested Amount in the Company on the Investment Date. The minimum initial investment is $20,000. An additional investment requires an updated Schedule A signed by both parties and has its own Investment Date and Lockup Period.\n\n**2.2 Conditions.** The Company accepts no funds until the Investor has delivered signed Schedules C and D, every form Securities Laws require, and the identification the Company requests. The Company is bound only when it has received cleared funds and signed this Agreement. It may refuse any investment and will return unaccepted money without return.\n\n**2.3 Investment contract only.** This Agreement is an investment contract. It is not a loan, deposit, promissory note or credit facility. The Investor receives no shares or right to shares, no ownership interest in the Company or its assets, no vote or part in management, and no share of profit, growth or sale proceeds beyond the Return and the Redemption Price. The Investor is not the Company's partner, co-owner, agent or employee. No one is the Investor's trustee or fiduciary.\n\n**2.4 Use of funds.** The Company may use the Invested Amount for any purpose of its business as a whole. It is not tied to any vehicle or asset, is not held in trust, and may be mixed with other money.\n\n**2.5 Other Investors.** The Company may raise any amount from Other Investors at any time, on different amounts, percentages and dates, without the Investor's consent. The Investor is not entitled to their terms.\n\n**2.6 Register.** The Company's register of investors, Invested Amounts, reinvestments and Transfers is conclusive, absent obvious error.\n\n## 3. Lockup and Return\n\n**3.1 Lockup.** No return is earned for the Lockup Period, whether during it or afterwards.\n\n**3.2 Return.** For each Return Month the Investment earns a return (the \"**Return**\") of one-twelfth of the Yearly Percentage multiplied by the Invested Amount at the start of that month, pro-rated by days for a part month. The Return is fixed: it does not vary with the Company's results and changes only by an updated Schedule A signed by both parties.\n\n**3.3 Payment.** Unless a Return is reinvested under section 4, the Company will pay it on its Payment Date by electronic transfer to the Investor's bank account in Schedule A, or another account in the Investor's name notified at least 10 days before. That payment discharges the Company.\n\n**3.4 Tax.** The Investor is responsible for all tax on the Investment, including on reinvested Returns. The Company gives no tax advice, may withhold what the law requires without gross-up, and may hold back payment until it has the tax information it needs.\n\n**3.5 Yearly rate.** For the *Interest Act* (Canada), and without admitting that the Return is interest, the yearly rate equivalent to the monthly Return is the Yearly Percentage.\n\n**3.6 Statements.** The Company will give the Investor a statement for each Return Month showing the Return, whether it was paid or reinvested, and the Invested Amount. The Investor has no other right to information or to inspect the Company's records, premises or vehicles.\n\n## 4. Reinvestment\n\n**4.1 Election.** The Investor may choose in Schedule A to have each Return added to the Invested Amount in place of being paid, and may change that choice by written notice. A change applies from the first Return Month that starts at least 10 days after the Company receives it.\n\n**4.2 Effect.** A reinvested Return is added to the Invested Amount on the last day of its Return Month, has no new Lockup Period, and cannot be withdrawn.\n\n**4.3 Suspension.** The Company may stop reinvestment going forward on 30 days' written notice, and will stop it if continuing would breach Securities Laws.\n\n## 5. No Fixed Term; No Right to Repayment\n\n**5.1 Term.** The Invested Amount stays invested with the Company. It is not repaid on any schedule, and no Return payment repays it. This Agreement has no fixed or maximum term.\n\n**5.2 No demand.** The Investor has no right, at any time or for any reason, to demand repayment, redemption or withdrawal of any part of the Invested Amount.\n\n**5.3 Exit.** The Investor may exit only by a Transfer under section 6 or a redemption or purchase under section 7.\n\n## 6. Transfer\n\n**6.1 Consent required.** A Transfer is void unless the Company consents in writing and the transferee delivers, in the form the Company requires, an agreement to be bound by this Agreement and signed Schedules A, C and D.\n\n**6.2 Consent.** The Company will not unreasonably withhold consent to a sale or assignment. It may always refuse a pledge or charge; a transferee who does not qualify under Securities Laws, cannot be identified or lawfully dealt with, or competes with or is in a dispute with the Company; and any Transfer while the Investor is in breach of this Agreement.\n\n**6.3 Terms.** The transferee may be an Other Investor or a new investor, and holds the Transferred part with the same Yearly Percentage, Investment Date and Lockup End Date from the effective date in the Company's consent. The price is a matter between the Investor and the transferee alone.\n\n**6.4 Death or incapacity.** If an individual Investor dies or becomes incapable, the Investment passes to the estate or legal representative on evidence the Company reasonably requires, without consent.\n\n**6.5 Resale restrictions.** The Investment is subject to resale restrictions under Securities Laws that may never expire, because the Company does not intend to become a reporting issuer. Complying with them on a Transfer is the Investor's responsibility.\n\n## 7. Redemption and Purchase by the Company\n\n**7.1 Redemption.** The Company may redeem all or part of the Investment at any time, including during the Lockup Period, on at least six months' written notice stating the amount and the Redemption Date, or on shorter notice agreed in writing. It may redeem the Investment without redeeming any Other Investor's investment, and the reverse.\n\n**7.2 Payment.** On the Redemption Date the Company will pay the Redemption Price under section 3.3. Neither party pays any premium, penalty or break fee.\n\n**7.3 Purchase on request.** After the Lockup Period the Investor may ask the Company in writing to buy any part of the Investment, at a price and date agreed in writing. The Company may refuse for any reason.\n\n**7.4 Effect.** On payment, the redeemed or purchased part of the Investment is cancelled. The Investor will sign a receipt and release on request.\n\n## 8. Ranking and Recourse\n\n**8.1 Unsecured.** The Investment is unsecured. The Investor has no charge, lien or other claim over any vehicle or other asset of the Company, and will register nothing against the Company or its assets.\n\n**8.2 Ranking.** The Investor's claims rank behind the Senior Obligations, equally and rateably with Other Investors, and ahead of distributions to the Company's shareholders and repayment of shareholder loans. A court or trustee may rank them differently.\n\n**8.3 Further debt.** The Company may borrow, lease or finance vehicles and grant security over any of its assets without the Investor's consent. The Investor will sign any postponement a holder of Senior Obligations reasonably requires.\n\n**8.4 No personal liability.** The Investor's only recourse is against the Company. No shareholder, director, officer, employee or affiliate of the Company, and no individual who controls any of them, guarantees or is personally liable for any obligation under this Agreement, except for that person's own fraud.\n\n**8.5 Missed payment.** If the Company does not pay a Return when due, the Investor's only remedy is to sue the Company for that amount. A missed payment does not make the Invested Amount due, does not override section 5.2, and gives no right against the Company's assets or any person named in section 8.4.\n\n**8.6 Winding up.** If the Company stops carrying on business, it will redeem the Investment, after the Senior Obligations and rateably with Other Investors, before any distribution to its shareholders.\n\n## 9. Representations\n\n**9.1 Investor's representations.** The Investor represents, on the Investment Date and on each additional investment, and will tell the Company promptly of any change, that the Investor:\n\n1. has the capacity and authority to sign this Agreement and, if an individual, is at least 18;\n2. resides, and is resident for tax purposes, where Schedule A says;\n3. is investing the Investor's own money, which does not come from crime, as principal, for investment and not for resale or for anyone else;\n4. fits the category initialled in Schedule D; and\n5. has given the Company only true and complete information.\n\n**9.2 Investor's acknowledgments.** The Investor acknowledges that:\n\n1. the Investment is, or is likely to be treated as, a security, sold without a prospectus in reliance on section 9.1 and Schedule D;\n2. no one has promised a resale, repurchase or refund of the Investment other than under this Agreement, or anything about its future value; and\n3. the Investor has relied only on this Agreement, any offering memorandum the Company delivered, and the Investor's own advisers, and not on any advertisement, projection or oral statement.\n\n**9.3 Indemnity and personal information.** The Investor will indemnify the Company for losses caused by an untrue representation of the Investor. The Investor consents to the Company using and disclosing the Investor's personal information to administer the Investment and meet legal, tax and regulatory obligations, including filings with securities regulators.\n\n**9.4 Company.** The Company represents, on the Investment Date, that it validly exists, has authorized this Agreement, which binds it and breaches none of its articles, by-laws or shareholders' or material agreements, and is neither a reporting issuer nor insolvent. While the Investment is outstanding, the Company will carry on business lawfully with the licences and insurance a prudent operator would keep, keep proper books, make the filings Securities Laws require, and promptly tell the Investor of its insolvency or an agreed sale of substantially all of its business.\n\n**9.5 No other representations.** The Company makes no other representation, including about its future results or ability to pay. Schedule B and any projection illustrate calculations only and promise nothing.\n\n## 10. General\n\n**10.1 Confidentiality.** Each party will keep confidential the terms of this Agreement and the other party's non-public information, except as required by law or a regulator, or to advisers, lenders, proposed transferees or buyers bound to keep it confidential.\n\n**10.2 Maximum lawful rate.** The parties do not intend this Agreement to advance credit. If a court nonetheless finds any amount payable under it to be interest at a criminal rate under section 347 of the *Criminal Code* (Canada), that amount is reduced retroactively to the highest lawful amount, first by reducing the Yearly Percentage. Any excess received is applied against the Invested Amount or refunded, at the Company's choice.\n\n**10.3 Set-off.** The Company may set off any amount the Investor owes it under this Agreement against any amount it owes the Investor.\n\n**10.4 Entire agreement.** This Agreement is the entire agreement about the Investment. It replaces all earlier discussions, term sheets, messages, advertisements and marketing material. Nothing in it limits a right under Securities Laws that cannot be waived.\n\n**10.5 Changes and assignment.** An amendment or waiver must be in writing and signed by the party bound. A change to an Other Investor's terms does not amend this Agreement. The Company may assign this Agreement to a successor or a buyer of its business. This Agreement binds each party's heirs, successors and permitted assigns.\n\n**10.6 Notices.** A notice must be in writing and sent by hand, courier or email to the address in Schedule A or one later notified.\n\n**10.7 Law and courts.** Ontario law, and the federal laws of Canada that apply there, govern this Agreement. The courts of Ontario sitting in Toronto have exclusive jurisdiction.\n\n**10.8 Other terms.** If any part of this Agreement is unenforceable, the rest continues in effect. Neither party is liable to the other for indirect, special or punitive damages, except for fraud. This Agreement may be signed in counterparts and electronically.\n\n## Signatures\n\n**{{company}}**, operating as CarmaCars\n\nBy: ______________________________  Name: [●]  Title: [●]  Date: [●]\n\n**Investor**\n\nSignature: ______________________________  Name: [●]  Title, if not an individual: [●]  Date: [●]\n\n## Schedule A: Investor Terms\n\n| Item | Details |\n| --- | --- |\n| Company's address and email for notices | [●] |\n| Investor's full legal name and type (individual, corporation, trust, other) | [●] |\n| Investor's residential or head office address, email and telephone | [●] |\n| Resident of Canada for tax purposes | Yes / No. If no, country: [●] |\n| Invested Amount (minimum $20,000) | $[●] |\n| Yearly Percentage | [●]% per year |\n| Investment Date | [●] |\n| Lockup End Date (six months after the Investment Date) | [●] |\n| Returns | ☐ Pay monthly  ☐ Reinvest |\n| Investor's bank account for payments | [●] |\n| Additional investments (amount, Investment Date, Lockup End Date, initials) | [●] |\n\nCompany: ______________________________  Date: [●]\n\nInvestor: ______________________________  Date: [●]\n\n## Schedule B: Worked Examples\n\nThese examples illustrate sections 3 and 4 only and are not a forecast. Both assume $20,000 invested on January 1, 2027 at a Yearly Percentage of 30%, with a Lockup End Date of July 1, 2027.\n\n**Example 1: Return paid monthly.** No Return is earned for January to June 2027. From July 2027 the monthly Return is $20,000 × 30% ÷ 12 = $500, first paid on August 15, 2027.\n\n**Example 2: Return reinvested for 12 months.** No cash is paid.\n\n| Return Month | Return reinvested | Invested Amount at month end |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1: July 2027 | $500.00 | $20,500.00 |\n| 2 | $512.50 | $21,012.50 |\n| 3 | $525.31 | $21,537.81 |\n| 4 | $538.45 | $22,076.26 |\n| 5 | $551.91 | $22,628.17 |\n| 6 | $565.70 | $23,193.87 |\n| 7 | $579.85 | $23,773.72 |\n| 8 | $594.34 | $24,368.06 |\n| 9 | $609.20 | $24,977.26 |\n| 10 | $624.43 | $25,601.69 |\n| 11 | $640.04 | $26,241.73 |\n| 12: June 2028 | $656.04 | $26,897.77 |\n\nIf the Investor then switches to payment, the monthly Return is $26,897.77 × 30% ÷ 12 = $672.44.\n\n## Schedule C: Risk Acknowledgment and Independent Legal Advice\n\n**WARNING: THIS IS A RISKY INVESTMENT. YOU COULD LOSE ALL THE MONEY YOU INVEST. INITIAL EACH STATEMENT ONLY IF YOU UNDERSTAND AND ACCEPT IT.**\n\n| Statement | Initials |\n| --- | --- |\n| I could lose all of my money. Nobody guarantees the Return or my Invested Amount. The Return is high because the risk is high. | [●] |\n| I cannot demand my money back. I can exit only by selling to an investor the Company accepts, or if the Company chooses to buy or redeem my Investment. I may have to hold indefinitely. | [●] |\n| I earn nothing for the first six months, and that is never made up. | [●] |\n| I am not an owner. I get no shares, no vote, no say in the business, and no share of its profits or of any sale. | [●] |\n| My Investment is unsecured and ranks behind the Company's lenders and other creditors. If the Company fails, I may get nothing. No shareholder, director or officer is personally liable to me. | [●] |\n| The Company is a new business with little or no operating history, exposed to accidents, theft, insurance costs, depreciation, regulation, competition and seasonal demand. It may not earn enough to pay the Return. | [●] |\n| The Company may raise unlimited amounts from other investors on different terms, take on debt that ranks ahead of me, and redeem my Investment on six months' notice, which ends my Return. | [●] |\n| If I reinvest, I receive no cash, my amount at risk grows, and I may owe tax on Returns I did not receive. | [●] |\n| No regulator has reviewed this Investment and no prospectus protects me. It is not a deposit and is not insured. The Company is not a registered dealer or adviser and has given me no investment, tax or suitability advice. | [●] |\n| I can bear the loss of my whole Invested Amount, and I have not borrowed to invest unless I have told the Company in writing. | [●] |\n\n**Independent legal advice.** The Company's lawyers act for the Company only. The Investor initials one:\n\n| Choice | Initials |\n| --- | --- |\n| I obtained independent legal advice from [●] of [●] before signing. | [●] |\n| I was advised to obtain independent legal advice, had enough time to do so, and chose not to. | [●] |\n\nI have read and understood this Agreement and am signing it voluntarily.\n\nInvestor: ______________________________  Name: [●]  Date: [●]\n\n## Schedule D: Exemption Certificate\n\nThe Investor certifies that the Investor fits the category initialled below. The Company relies on this certificate to sell the Investment without a prospectus.\n\n| Category | Also required | Initials |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Accredited investor** under Securities Laws. Paragraph of the definition: [●] | Form 45-106F9 if required for an individual; proof of income or assets | [●] |\n| **Offering memorandum exemption, eligible investor.** I received the Company's offering memorandum. Including this Investment, I have invested under this exemption in the past 12 months no more than $30,000, or $100,000 on suitability advice from a portfolio manager, investment dealer or exempt market dealer. | Form 45-106F4 with Schedules 1 and 2; a copy of any suitability advice | [●] |\n\nInvestor: ______________________________  Name: [●]  Date: [●]\n\n**Company use only.** Exemption relied on: [●]. Steps taken to verify: [●]. Report of exempt distribution filed on: [●].\n";
export const VA_MD = "This agreement is between {{company}}, operating as CarmaCars (\"CarmaCars\"), and the contractor named in Schedule A (\"you\"). It starts on the Start Date in Schedule A.\n\n## 1. Status\n\n1.1 You are an independent contractor. You are not an employee, partner or agent of CarmaCars and cannot sign for it or bind it.\n\n1.2 You supply your own equipment, internet and workspace, and you pay your own taxes and insurance and follow the laws where you live.\n\n1.3 You do the work yourself. You may not subcontract it or let anyone else use your access.\n\n1.4 You may work for other clients, but not for another vehicle rental business that serves Ontario while this agreement runs.\n\n## 2. Services and standards\n\n2.1 You provide the services for your role in Schedule A (the \"Services\") during the Coverage Hours.\n\n2.2 You will:\n\n- follow CarmaCars' written procedures and instructions, as updated from time to time (\"Procedures\");\n- work accurately, honestly and on time;\n- deal with customers, vehicle owners and suppliers only through CarmaCars' accounts, phone numbers and templates;\n- make no promise, discount or statement about price, insurance or coverage that the Procedures do not allow; and\n- tell CarmaCars promptly about any error, complaint or missed deadline.\n\n2.3 You record your time and tasks in the system CarmaCars names. CarmaCars may monitor and record everything done in its systems, including calls and messages.\n\n## 3. Pay\n\n3.1 CarmaCars pays the Rate in Schedule A for time you worked, recorded and CarmaCars approved. Payment is made by the Payment Method, at the times in Schedule A.\n\n3.2 The Rate is your whole payment. There are no benefits, overtime, vacation pay, commissions or expenses unless CarmaCars agrees in writing first.\n\n3.3 CarmaCars may deduct from any payment an amount you owe it under this agreement.\n\n## 4. Confidentiality and data\n\n4.1 \"Confidential Information\" means everything not public that you learn through the Services. It includes personal information about customers and owners (\"Personal Data\"), pricing, Procedures, financial records, supplier and insurance terms, and material belonging to CarmaCars' franchisor.\n\n4.2 You will use Confidential Information only to perform the Services and disclose it to no one outside CarmaCars. This duty continues after this agreement ends. If a law forces disclosure, you will tell CarmaCars first where the law allows.\n\n4.3 You will:\n\n- reach Personal Data only through the systems and accounts CarmaCars gives you (\"Systems\"), and only as a task requires;\n- not copy, download, export, screenshot, photograph or forward any customer or owner list or Personal Data to a personal device, a personal account or any other person;\n- never write down or store payment card numbers anywhere, and enter them only into CarmaCars' payment system;\n- work only on a password-locked device with current software, never on a public or shared computer;\n- use a unique strong password and two-step verification on every account, and share logins with no one; and\n- report any actual or suspected loss, unauthorized access or misuse of data, an account or a device (a \"Data Incident\") to CarmaCars within 24 hours of discovering it, and help contain it.\n\n4.4 You will sign the franchisor's non-disclosure agreement if asked. The franchisor may enforce this section 4 directly for its own material.\n\n## 5. Money controls\n\n5.1 This section applies whenever your role touches CarmaCars' money. CarmaCars' money and accounts are used only for its business and only as the Procedures allow.\n\n5.2 You will not make or approve any payout, refund, credit, deposit release or other payment that is outside the Procedures or above the Single Limit in Schedule A. A payment above the Dual Approval Threshold in Schedule A needs written approval from the Approver before it is made.\n\n5.3 You will not:\n\n- change a payee's banking details without the Approver's written approval;\n- pay yourself or anyone connected to you, other than your approved pay under section 3;\n- move money to an account that is not CarmaCars'; or\n- take money personally from a customer, owner or supplier.\n\n5.4 Every entry must be accurate and backed by a document. You report any discrepancy or suspected fraud the same day. CarmaCars may audit your work at any time.\n\n## 6. Work product, referrals and non-solicitation\n\n6.1 Everything you create or collect in the Services belongs to CarmaCars from the moment it exists. This includes records, content, listings, leads, contact lists, templates and any account or profile opened for the Services. You assign all rights in it to CarmaCars and waive your moral rights.\n\n6.2 You earn no referral fee, kickback or commission on any renter, owner or booking. You accept no gift or payment from a customer, owner or supplier.\n\n6.3 While this agreement runs and for 12 months after it ends, you will not, for yourself or anyone else:\n\n- solicit or divert any customer or owner you dealt with or learned of through the Services to rent or list a vehicle elsewhere; or\n- solicit any CarmaCars staff member or contractor to stop working with CarmaCars.\n\n## 7. Ending this agreement\n\n7.1 Either party may end this agreement on 7 days' written notice. During the Trial Period, either party may end it at once.\n\n7.2 CarmaCars may end it at once, without notice, if you breach section 4, 5 or 6, act dishonestly, repeatedly miss Coverage Hours or commit any other serious breach.\n\n7.3 CarmaCars may suspend your access to the Systems at any time.\n\n7.4 When this agreement ends, you stop using the Systems, hand over every password and account, return or delete all Confidential Information and confirm in writing that you have done so. CarmaCars pays for approved time up to the end date and owes nothing more.\n\n7.5 Sections 4, 6 and 8 continue after this agreement ends.\n\n## 8. General\n\n8.1 The laws of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that apply there govern this agreement. Disputes go to the courts of Ontario. CarmaCars may also ask any court for an urgent order to stop a breach of section 4, 5 or 6.\n\n8.2 This is the whole agreement on its subject. Between you and CarmaCars it prevails over the hiring platform's terms where they permit. Changes must be in writing and accepted by both parties, except that CarmaCars may update the Procedures by notice.\n\n8.3 If part of this agreement cannot be enforced, the rest stands. You may not transfer this agreement. CarmaCars may.\n\n8.4 This agreement is signed through an electronic signature service, and electronic signatures are valid. Notices go by email to the addresses in Schedule A.\n\n8.5 You confirm that you have read and understood this agreement and had the chance to get advice.\n\n**{{company}}, operating as CarmaCars**\nBy: [●], [●] (title). Date: [●]\n\n**Contractor**\nName: [●]. Signature: [●]. Date: [●]\n\n## Schedule A\n\n| Item | Term |\n| --- | --- |\n| Contractor | [●] (legal name), [●] (country), [●] (email) |\n| Role | [●] (one of the four roles below) |\n| Coverage Hours (Toronto time) | [●] (days and times), [●] hours a week |\n| Rate | [●] an hour, in [●] (currency) |\n| Start Date | [●] |\n| CarmaCars notice email | [●] |\n| Payment Method | Through [●] (hiring platform) |\n| Payment timing | [●] (weekly, every two weeks or monthly) |\n| Trial Period | First [●] days |\n| Single Limit (finance role) | [●] per payment |\n| Dual Approval Threshold (finance role) | [●] per payment |\n| Approver | [●] |\n\n**Duties by role**\n\n- **Finance and Billing Coordinator.** Weekly bookkeeping. Per-car revenue and cost calculations for owner statements. Insurance and management fee billing to owners. Owner payouts. Customer invoicing. Toll and ticket entry matched to bookings. Billing extra kilometres, damage and fuel before a deposit is released. The monthly fleet report to the franchisor on the 1st.\n- **Fleet Operations Coordinator.** Scheduling for each car. Coordinating field staff for detailing, delivery and handoffs. Reviewing check-in and check-out photos for damage, kilometres and fuel. General administration.\n- **Customer Service and Growth Coordinator.** Inbound calls and emails. Posting rentals and the owner program on classified sites and social media. Outreach to recruit car owners.\n- **Sales.** Following up leads and enquiries. Quoting rates as the Procedures allow. Turning enquiries into bookings. Outreach to business and long-term rental customers.\n";
export const FIELD_MD = "This agreement is between {{company}}, operating as CarmaCars (\"CarmaCars\"), and the employee named in Schedule A (\"you\"). It starts on the Start Date in Schedule A.\n\n## 1. Employment\n\n1.1 You are an employee of CarmaCars in the role in Schedule A. The Employment Standards Act, 2000 (\"ESA\") applies, and where it gives you more than this agreement, the ESA governs.\n\n1.2 Your hours vary with bookings and none are guaranteed. CarmaCars schedules your shifts.\n\n1.3 You cannot sign for CarmaCars or bind it, except to complete handover documents as the Procedures require.\n\n## 2. Duties\n\n2.1 You perform the jobs CarmaCars assigns by WhatsApp or its app (each a \"Job\") for the role in Schedule A. You follow CarmaCars' written procedures, as updated from time to time (\"Procedures\"). A \"Vehicle\" is any vehicle CarmaCars asks you to handle. Vehicles belong to third-party owners.\n\n2.2 Your Jobs include:\n\n- **Delivery and pickup.** Move the Vehicle to or from the customer at the assigned time and place, and tell CarmaCars at once if you will be late.\n- **Identity check.** Before you release a Vehicle, check each driver's original licence against the person and the booking, and photograph it as the Procedures require. Do not release the Vehicle if the licence is expired or does not match, or if the person seems impaired. Call CarmaCars instead.\n- **Handover.** Have the customer sign the handover record.\n- **Photo inspection.** At every handover and return, take time-stamped photos from the fixed angles in the Procedures and upload them before you leave. The minimum is each corner, each side, each wheel, the windshield, the roof, the front and rear interior, the trunk and the dashboard.\n- **Fuel and odometer.** Record the fuel or charge level and the odometer reading in the app at every handover and return.\n- **Detailing.** Clean the Vehicle to the standard in the Procedures and hand any lost property to CarmaCars.\n- **Damage reports.** Report new damage, warning lights, missing items, smoke odour or signs of misuse, with photos, before the Vehicle is moved again.\n\n## 3. Licence and driving record\n\n3.1 You confirm that you hold a full Ontario Class G licence, have held it for the period in Schedule A, may legally work in Canada, and have a driving record that CarmaCars' insurer accepts.\n\n3.2 You give CarmaCars a current driver's abstract before you start and whenever it asks. You consent to CarmaCars and its insurer checking your licence and record.\n\n3.3 You must tell CarmaCars immediately, and before you drive a Vehicle again, about:\n\n- any suspension, restriction or expiry of your licence, including a roadside suspension;\n- any driving-related charge or conviction, and any criminal charge;\n- any collision in which you were the driver; and\n- anything that makes you unfit to drive safely.\n\n3.4 You do not drive a Vehicle while your licence is not valid, while you are unfit, or after CarmaCars' insurer declines to cover you.\n\n## 4. Vehicle rules\n\n4.1 You drive a Vehicle only for an assigned Job, by a direct route, and only if it is a type authorized in Schedule A. You never use a Vehicle for personal trips or errands, and you never let anyone else drive it.\n\n4.2 While a Vehicle is in your charge, you:\n\n- obey all traffic and parking laws;\n- have no alcohol, cannabis or other impairing drug in your body;\n- do not hold or use a phone while driving, set navigation before you move, and answer messages only when parked;\n- do not smoke or vape in or beside the Vehicle;\n- carry no passengers, pets or personal cargo unless CarmaCars approves in writing;\n- never leave it unlocked, running or with the key inside; and\n- give the key only to the named renter or to CarmaCars.\n\n4.3 Every Vehicle has a GPS tracker that records location, speed, route and driving events at all times. You consent to CarmaCars collecting this information, and the photos and messages you send, to manage Jobs, investigate incidents, deal with insurers, owners and authorities, and enforce this agreement. You do not tamper with a tracker.\n\n## 5. Tickets, accidents and damage\n\n5.1 **Tickets.** You are responsible for every traffic, parking, toll and camera fine incurred while a Vehicle is in your charge, unless it results from CarmaCars' instruction. You pay or dispute each fine before it is due. If CarmaCars pays it, you owe CarmaCars that amount.\n\n5.2 **Accidents.** After any collision, theft or injury, you stop, make the scene safe, call 911 where anyone is hurt or the law requires, and call CarmaCars at once. You take photos and the other party's details, and you do not admit fault, settle or sign anything. You give CarmaCars a written report within 24 hours and cooperate with the insurer and the police.\n\n5.3 **Damage.** You are responsible for loss or damage, including the insurance deductible and uninsured costs, caused by your gross negligence, wilful misconduct, impaired driving, unauthorized use or breach of section 3 or 4. You are not responsible for an ordinary accident that happens while you follow this agreement.\n\n5.4 **Recovery.** CarmaCars does not deduct tickets, fines or Vehicle loss or damage from your wages. An amount you owe under this section 5 is a debt, which CarmaCars may recover only where the law allows.\n\n## 6. Customers and confidentiality\n\n6.1 With customers you are polite and professional. You do not argue, harass or discriminate, and you contact a customer only about a Job. You refer questions about price, insurance or fault to CarmaCars. You take no cash or payment from a customer, and you never offer a private rental or side service.\n\n6.2 \"Confidential Information\" means everything not public that you learn through your work. It includes customer and owner names, addresses, identification and licence details, Vehicle locations, pricing, Procedures, and material belonging to CarmaCars' franchisor.\n\n6.3 You use Confidential Information only for a Job and disclose it to no one, during and after this agreement. You delete identification photos and customer details from your phone once they are uploaded and keep no copies. You post nothing online about customers or Vehicles. You report a lost phone or any leak to CarmaCars within 24 hours. You sign the franchisor's non-disclosure agreement if asked.\n\n6.4 For 12 months after this agreement ends, you do not solicit any customer or owner you dealt with to rent or list a vehicle elsewhere.\n\n## 7. Referral commission\n\n7.1 You earn a referral fee of 20% of the Rental Charge on the first completed rental of a renter you referred. Later rentals by that renter earn nothing. The fee is a commission and part of your wages.\n\n7.2 The \"Rental Charge\" is the rental rate CarmaCars collects and keeps for that rental, after discounts and refunds and before tax. It excludes taxes, deposits, protection products, delivery charges and charges for fuel, kilometres, tolls, tickets and damage.\n\n7.3 A referral counts only if:\n\n- the renter has never booked or enquired with CarmaCars before;\n- your referral code or name is entered on the booking when it is made; and\n- no one else was recorded as the referrer first.\n\nCarmaCars' booking record decides who referred a renter, unless it contains an obvious error.\n\n7.4 The fee is earned when the rental is completed and paid in full, and is paid on the next Pay Date. It is not earned on a booking that is cancelled, refunded, unpaid or charged back, on your own rental or one by a member of your household, or on a booking made after this agreement ends.\n\n7.5 You promote CarmaCars truthfully and only as the Procedures allow. CarmaCars may change or end the referral fee on 30 days' written notice, for bookings made after that notice period.\n\n## 8. Pay and hours\n\n8.1 **Wage.** CarmaCars pays the Hourly Wage in Schedule A for all hours you work, on the Pay Dates, less the deductions the law requires for income tax, Canada Pension Plan and Employment Insurance. Your pay is never less than the ESA minimum wage.\n\n8.2 **Vacation pay.** You agree that CarmaCars pays your vacation pay, at 4% of your wages, on each Pay Date and shows it separately on your pay statement. You may take the vacation time the ESA gives you.\n\n8.3 **Hours.** You record your start and end times and your Jobs in the app. Your hours of work, rest and eating periods, public holidays and leaves follow the ESA. Overtime needs CarmaCars' approval beforehand. It is paid at 1.5 times your Hourly Wage for each hour over 44 in a week.\n\n8.4 **Expenses.** CarmaCars repays expenses it approved beforehand, such as fuel, parking and transit, when you give it the receipt.\n\n## 9. Ending your employment\n\n9.1 You may resign on 7 days' written notice.\n\n9.2 CarmaCars may end your employment by giving you the notice or termination pay, and any other entitlement, that the ESA requires, and nothing more. CarmaCars gives no notice or pay only where the ESA permits that.\n\n9.3 CarmaCars may stop assigning you driving Jobs at any time for safety or insurance reasons.\n\n9.4 When your employment ends, you return every key, fob and item of equipment at once and delete all Confidential Information. CarmaCars pays all wages you earned to the end date, including referral fees and vacation pay, within the time the ESA requires. Sections 5, 6 and 10 continue.\n\n## 10. General\n\n10.1 The laws of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that apply there govern this agreement. Disputes go to the courts of Ontario.\n\n10.2 This is the whole agreement on its subject. Changes must be in writing and accepted by both parties, except that CarmaCars may update the Procedures by notice.\n\n10.3 If part of this agreement cannot be enforced, the rest stands. This agreement is signed through an electronic signature service, and electronic signatures are valid.\n\n10.4 You confirm that you understood this agreement and had the chance to get advice.\n\n**{{company}}, operating as CarmaCars**\nBy: [●], [●] (title). Date: [●]\n\n**Employee**\nName: [●]. Signature: [●]. Date: [●]\n\n## Schedule A\n\n| Item | Term |\n| --- | --- |\n| Employee | [●] (legal name), [●] (address), [●] (phone), [●] (email) |\n| Driver's licence | Ontario Class G, number [●] |\n| Role | [●] (driver, detailer, or driver and detailer) |\n| Hourly Wage | $[●] an hour |\n| Start Date | [●] |\n| Vehicle types authorized | [●] |\n| Referral code | [●] |\n| Pay Dates | [●] (weekly, every two weeks or twice a month) |\n| Minimum licence period | Full Class G held for at least [●] years |\n";
